WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.630
Charge a capacitor to 9 volts.

2
00:00:02.680 --> 00:00:06.530
Then connect it across a
resistor, and let it discharge.

3
00:00:06.580 --> 00:00:09.320
As charge leaves, the voltage falls.

4
00:00:09.370 --> 00:00:10.940
So the current falls.

5
00:00:10.990 --> 00:00:13.240
So the charge leaves more slowly.

6
00:00:13.290 --> 00:00:15.680
The curve flattens and flattens.

7
00:00:15.730 --> 00:00:18.520
In this model, it gets
ever closer to zero,

8
00:00:18.570 --> 00:00:20.130
but never reaches it.

9
00:00:20.180 --> 00:00:23.520
So what sets how fast it approaches empty?

10
00:00:23.570 --> 00:00:27.850
In this mission, you'll follow a
capacitor step by step as it charges,

11
00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:30.860
and see why the current falls as it fills.

12
00:00:30.910 --> 00:00:35.050
Then you'll sketch six graphs
of charge, voltage and current,

13
00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:37.790
and read what their slopes and areas mean.

14
00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:42.450
Your mission: find out what sets
the pace of a discharging capacitor.
